# Effective .dockerignore for the Write API build (context = `backend/`).
#
# Docker only reads the .dockerignore at the context root. The Write API
# Dockerfile uses `backend/` as its context, so this file — not the one
# next to the Dockerfile at `backend/write-api/.dockerignore` — is what
# the daemon actually consults when packing the build context.
#
# Critically excludes `**/obj/`: a host-side `dotnet restore` leaves
# `project.assets.json` and `*.nuget.g.props` behind that reference
# Windows-only NuGet fallback folders (e.g. `C:\Program Files (x86)\
# Microsoft Visual Studio\Shared\NuGetPackages`). If those leak into
# the Linux container, the in-container build fails with:
#   error MSB4018: NuGet.Packaging.Core.PackagingException:
#   Unable to find fallback package folder '...'.

# Build outputs — must stay excluded, see note above.
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/TestResults/

# Local tooling caches and IDE state
**/.vs/
**/.idea/
**/.vscode/
**/*.user
**/*.suo

# Things irrelevant to the backend image build
**/.git/
**/.github/
**/.claude/
**/dev_env/
**/testing/
**/docs/
**/infrastructure/

# Front-end source (the Write API image does not bundle the SPA)
**/node_modules/
**/dist/

# Never bake local secrets into images
**/.env
**/.env.local
**/.env.*.local
